  "query_preview": "(Sunday through Wednesday)...\nHigh pressure will slowly weaken into the middle of next week. The\naxis of the high pressure will move northward just enough for the\nmid level flow across the area to become more easterly by the\nmiddle of next week. High temperatures for inland areas will\ndecrease around 5 degrees from Saturday through Wednesday while\nsurface dewpoints for inland areas will slowly increase with\nhumidity slowing increasing. \n\nWarm sea surface temperatures in the mid 70s, around 5 degrees \nabove average, will maintain higher humidity for coastal areas \ninto the western valleys. Low temperatures will change little, \nranging from a few degrees above average for the coast into the \nwestern valleys with the mountains and deserts 5 to 10 degrees \nabove average.\n\nHigh temperatures for next Wednesday will range from around 80\nnear the coast to the mid 90s to 105 for the Inland Empire with \n110 to 114 for the lower deserts. Low temperatures for the coast\nand valleys will be mostly in the mid 60s to lower 70s, in the \n70s for the Apple and Lucerne Valleys, and in the mid 80s to lower\n90s for the lower deserts.\n\nHeatRisk will slowly decrease with HeatRisk for Wednesday of next\nweek moderate to major for the deserts, and mostly moderate for \nthe inland valleys, higher coastal terrain, and mountain areas \nbelow 7000 feet.",
